From 9f2233f75f79b4df410741ed95b4a7d17a6327dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:41:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/37] drm/gma500: add sgxfive transfer contexts

Add CREATE_CONTEXT and DESTROY_CONTEXT for transfer contexts. A context is a
firmware HW transfer context with its own 64 KiB client CCB and control page
in kernel memory the EDM reads through its own page directory, initialised
with its VM's page directory, and it holds a reference on that VM. The
first context boots the firmware if it is not running. Closing the file tears
contexts down before VMs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
